title: karr pick --json prints a plain sentence when there is nothing to pick
updated: 2026-08-10T02:25:30Z
---

Both no-result paths in `Cmd/Pick.pm` (`:134` and `:165`) print a sentence and
ignore `--json`:

    karr pick --claim me --json        -> "No available tasks to pick."  rc=0
    karr pick --claim me --json | jq . -> parse error

Every other command honours it: `list --json` on an empty board prints `[]`,
`archive` on an already-archived task prints `{"note":"already archived",...}`,
`show`/`log` print `[]`.

`pick` is *the* agent-facing command, so the one place JSON is guaranteed to be
machine-parsed is the one place it breaks.

Fix: emit `{"picked":null}` (or `null`) on the empty path. Worth a parity
decision at the same time: kanban-md returns a `NothingToPick` error with a
nonzero exit; karr returns 0, so an agent currently has to parse stdout to tell
"nothing to do" from "picked something".
